  "bad_tail_text": "NotImplementedError` stubs in `BloomFilter.add` and `BloomFilter.maybe`.\n\nunicaa01_p39_panic/main.py\n```\n\"\"\"Simple bloom filter.\"\"\"\nclass BloomFilter:\n    def __init__(self, size: int):\n        self.size = size\n        self.bits = [False] * size\n\n    def add(self, item: str):\n        hash1 = hash(item) % self.size\n        hash2 = (hash(item) // self.size) % self.size\n        self.bits[hash1] = True\n        self.bits[hash2] = True\n\n    def maybe(self, item: str) -> bool:\n        hash1 = hash(item) % self.size\n        hash2 = (hash(item) // self.size) % self.size\n        return self.bits[hash1] and self.bits[hash2]\n\ndef demo():\n    b = BloomFilter(64)\n    b.add(\"x\")\n    return b.maybe(\"x\")\n```\n\nThis implementation uses a simple bloom filter with two hash functions. The `add` method sets the bits corresponding to the hash values of the item to `True`. The `maybe` method checks if both bits are `True` and returns `True` if they are, indicating the item might be in the filter. The `demo` function demonstrates adding an item and checking if it might be in the filter.",
